-- NEGATIVE fixture for the future D-CYCLE check (spec §6.4.2, §6.3.7).
--
-- p2, NULLARY arm. The same mutual recursion as
-- cycle-p2-mutual-parameterised.l4 with the parameters removed:
--
--     `the left total`  reads  `the right total`
--     `the right total` reads  `the left total`
--
-- Nullary decides stay DECISIONS under Phase 4/5, so this cycle lives on the
-- informationRequirement graph (§6.3.7), not on the knowledgeRequirement graph
-- (§6.3.9) that its parameterised twin lands in. Two graphs, two detectors, two
-- fixtures.
--
-- Nothing here is recursive BY INSPECTION: each body names the other, neither
-- names itself, and no parameter shrinks. That is exactly §6.4.2's argument for
-- why the check has to be an SCC rather than an own-name-mention test.
--
-- Expected after Phase 4: one D-CYCLE over an SCC of size 2.
--
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THIS HEADER. The .l4 source was typechecked (`l4 check`, clean)
-- when it was written on 2026-07-31, with a prebuilt CLI. The statements above
-- about what TODAY'S EXPORTER emits and reports are taken from spec
-- §6.4.2/§6.4.5's table and were NOT re-measured here: that session had no
-- build. Whoever wires these fixtures into jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs must MEASURE
-- the expectation rather than transcribe it.
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `mutual recursion, nullary`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the left total` MEANS
    `the right total` PLUS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the right total` MEANS
    `the left total` PLUS 1
